* text=auto eol=lf
# Firmware images for the browser installer. "text=auto" guesses, and a
# guess that goes the wrong way on a megabyte of application image rewrites
# every CRLF inside it and produces a binary that flashes cleanly and does
# not boot. Nothing about that failure would point back at this file, so the
# images are declared binary rather than detected as binary.
*.bin     binary
*.png     binary
# The stock display skins on /skins (site 1.3.17), in static/skins/: a zip
# guessed as text would have its JPEGs rewritten, and unpack as broken
# pictures on somebody's card.
*.zip     binary
# The pitch's display faces (site 1.2.9), in static/fonts/.
*.woff    binary
*.ttf     binary
# The vendored browser installer, one directory per version, is kept byte for
# byte as npm published it, so SHA256SUMS beside it stays checkable. Declared binary: no line ending is
# ever rewritten in it, and git never tries to show a diff of a minified line.
vendor/esp-web-tools/*/*  binary
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
